 "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step5-opus-aa-1017-omp36-aa/omp-36/cells/aa-2/trig-omp-reported/24/workspace", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "aa-2", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/17.3.8 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/5347ff91e8f44f2c69a79d7b152b7301687cd5c8/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Python 3.13 \u2192 `datetime.fromisoformat` handles `Z` and offsets natively; naive inputs stay naive.\nI fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`. It now uses `datetime.fromisoformat(s)` instead of `strptime` with a fixed format. On Python 3.13, `fromisoformat` handles the `Z` suffix and offsets like `+02:00`. All 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` pass, including `test_naive` and `test_day_key`.\n\nTwo behaviour changes to know about:\n- **Timezone-aware results:** inputs with `Z` or an offset now give a timezone-aware datetime (UTC for `Z`). Inputs without a zone still give a naive one. Comparing or subtracting aware and naive datetimes raises a `TypeError`, so any caller that mixes both will need to handle that.\n- **Looser input:** `fromisoformat` accepts more ISO forms than the old fixed format, such as date-only strings and fractional seconds. Inputs that used to raise an error may now parse.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 51559, "requests_cache_wri